        "title": "Cooking the stew",
        "summary": "Raw chicken, potatoes, onion wedges, tomato and bay leaves go into the pot with salt and pepper and no added liquid. It is then cooked at high pressure for 15 minutes, with notes for both electric and stovetop pressure cookers and on quick release.",
        "first_segment": 1,
        "last_segment": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "Science of pressure cooking",
        "summary": "Explains how pressure raises the boiling point to about 240-250°F and how the rule that reaction rates double every 10°C makes 15 minutes roughly equal to an hour of braising.",
