        "segment_id": "kenji:-riGSANPe3g:s0002",
        "note": "Kenji says the written recipe calls for 25 minutes at pressure, but 15 minutes is plenty."
      },
      {
        "segment_id": "kenji:-riGSANPe3g:s0004",
        "note": "After stating that reaction rates double for every 10 degrees, he clarifies that this means 10 degrees Celsius, not Fahrenheit."
      },
      {
        "segment_id": "kenji:-riGSANPe3g:s0005",
        "note": "He first equates a 40°F rise with about 10°C, then restates it as 20°C and four times as fast. The 40°F rise is what he uses to say 15 minutes at pressure equals about an hour of braising."
      }
